    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` \u2014 passing; the other two test files are the abstract `AcceptanceBase` and its support).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is built from the generated `OwnerDto`, which is produced from `openapi.yml` and populated by `OwnerMapper`. To add `checkDigit`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `checkDigit` property (integer, 0\u20139) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a derived-value helper matching the existing `MembershipLevel`/`IdentityKey`/`Locality` pattern. Its `of(Owner)` computes the Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode` using the exact right-to-left, double-every-second-digit-from-the-rightmost algorithm the test replicates, returning `null` when there's no customer code.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(...CheckDigit.of(owner))\")` alongside the other derived-field mappings.\n\nThe test recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts it equals the returned `checkDigit`; my helper mirrors that algorithm exactly, so the two agree.",
